    "https://www.goshen.edu/employment/assistant-or-associate-professor-of-mathematics-computer-science-or-data-science/": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Mathematics, Computer Science, or Data Science",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Mathematics, Computer Science, or Data Science - Goshen College Skip to Main Content Language Toggle Search Toggle Search our site Search Menu Menu Toggle Apply Get Info Visit Give New Students Parents & Families Alumni Community Academics Menu Toggle Undergraduate Programs Graduate and Licensure Programs Honors Program Global Engagement Academic Dean’s Office Registrar’s Office Admissions and Aid Menu Toggle Undergraduate Admissions Graduate & Licensure Admissions Financial Aid Scholarships Net Price Calculator Visit Athletics Menu Toggle Recruiting Maple Leaf Athletic Club Watch Live Give to MLAC Student Life Menu Toggle Campus Housing Dining Clubs and Extracurriculars Campus Ministries Campus Safety Center for Health & Wellness About Menu Toggle Who We Are News and Events Facilities and Centers Employment Give to Goshen College Contact Us and Campus Directory Employment Open Position Assistant or Associate Professor of Mathematics, Computer Science, or Data Science Apply Here Goshen College is a Christian liberal arts institution that prepares students to thrive in life, leadership and service. We strive to model an inclusive community committed to transformative justice, peace, and sustainability. A respect and appreciation of the Anabaptist- Mennonite faith perspective and practices, and a commitment to the mission, vision, core values and community standards of Goshen College, are important for teaching and administrative faculty members. Position Summary: Goshen College invites applications for a full-time appointment as Assistant or Associate Professor of Mathematics, Computer Science, or Data Science with expertise in one or more of the three disciplines starting July 2027. Leadership as Department Chair (with associated stipend or course release) is available for candidates with prior  teaching and administrative experience seeking appointment at the Associate Professor level. Primary teaching responsibilities will be in the areas of mathematics, computer science, and/or data science as well as updating current curriculum to reflect future trends in the fields. In addition to teaching, the position includes recruiting, advising, and mentoring an increasingly culturally, racially and religiously diverse student body and supporting departmental co-curriculars. The mathematics and computer science department offers majors in Computer Science and Mathematics as well as minors in Computer Science, Game Development, and Mathematics. We plan to launch a Data Science major and minor in 2027-28. The department also offers some lower-level courses to serve students majoring in other disciplines. All faculty members have opportunities to develop courses within their expertise. Goshen College is a teaching college and the courses you will teach are spread across two semesters and a May term (e.g., 4 courses in Fall, 3 in Spring, and 1 during May Term). All teaching faculty serve on institution-wide committees and assist with advising (although not usually during the first year), as well as recruiting prospective students. The successful candidate must be ready to contribute to our strong tradition of excellence in scholarship as well as teaching. Candidates must be interested in working closely with students and fellow faculty members as part of a small, vibrant campus and community. Teaching Profile & Course Flexibility: The department serves students across Mathematics, Computer Science, and Data Science. Teaching assignments are flexible and collaboratively arranged based on candidate expertise, departmental needs, and interest. Successful candidates will teach a portfolio of courses across one or more of the following areas: Mathematics: Foundational and upper-level courses. We have a strong departmental preference for candidates capable of teaching upper-level pure and applied mathematics (e.g., Abstract Algebra, Modern Geometry, Differential Equations, Linear Algebra, and/or Calculus-based Probability & Statistics). Data Science: Introductory and emerging coursework for our new major/minor launching in 2027–28 (e.g., Introduction to Data Science, Data Visualization, Predictive Modeling, Machine Learning/AI, and Capstone Projects). Computer Science: Core and applied topics depending on background (e.g., Programming, Discrete Structures, Database Design, Web Applications, Systems Analysis, or Software Project Management). Candidates are not expected to cover all areas, but should demonstrate a strong interest in teaching core mathematics alongside topics in CS or Data Science, with opportunities to expand teaching breadth over time. For those with interdisciplinary interests, there are also opportunities to teach courses in the innovative general education and global studies program, including community-engaged and service-oriented courses. Essential Functions: Prepare course syllabi for assigned courses in collaboration with department chair and  academic dean Teach assigned courses with appropriate active and engaged learning practices Oversee student internships Mentor students through advising and recruiting activities Develop new courses and curriculum for the program Participate in department, school and college meetings Pursue appropriate professional development opportunities, including scholarly activities Complete other assigned duties Supervisory Responsibility: Students in assigned courses Student workers in department as needed Department faculty (for candidates interested in the Department Chair role) Education and Experience: Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in Mathematics, Computer Science, Data Science, or a closely related field (completed by August 2027) Demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching, active learning, and student mentorship Commitment to working effectively with culturally, racially, and religiously diverse student populations Alignment with and commitment to the mission and core values of Goshen College Preferred preparation Ph.D. in Mathematics, Computer Science, Data Science, or a closely related field (completed by August 2027) Experience in course and curriculum development relevant to mathematics, computer science, or data science Demonstrated experience teaching and mentoring diverse college students Administrative or academic leadership experience (for candidates interested in the Department Chair role) Core Competencies and Skills: Pedagogy & Technology: Strong aptitude in active learning practices and educational technology across undergraduate courses. Discipline Knowledge: Broad understanding of current career paths and emerging trends in mathematics, computer science, and data science. Scholarship & Mentorship: Active engagement in relevant scholarship and interest in mentoring student research or capstone projects. Collaboration & Communication: Excellent interpersonal, public speaking, and relationship-building skills to collaborate across departments and participate in college service. Work Environment/Environmental Conditions: Mostly inside/office conditions; Temperatures are usually moderate; Artificial lighting; Some exposure to dust and molds. Must use stairs or elevators to use toilet facilities. Using computers and other office equipment; moving around campus, inside and outside. All of the essential job functions are subject to reasonable accommodation. All job requirements listed indicate the minimum level of knowledge, skills and/or ability deemed necessary to perform the job proficiently. This job description is not to be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities or requirements. Individuals may be required to perform other job-related instructions as requested by the supervisor, subject to reasonable accommodation. This position description is not all-inclusive and may change at the option of the department head. Any major change will result in the position being reviewed for reclassification. Benefits: Healthcare/Prescription insurance (Goshen College pays employee premium) Dental insurance Vision insurance Flexible Spending Account Life/AD&D (Goshen College pays employee premium) Long Term Disability (after 1 year of employment – college pays employee premium) Retirement (403(b)) College contribution to retirement after 90 days Free membership to GC Recreation-Fitness Center Paid holidays Paid Parental Leave Tuition discounts and more Application Process & Timeline: Application materials may be attached to the Administrative & Teaching Faculty Application or sent electronically to [email protected] . Review of applications will begin on November 16, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Complete the online Administrative & Teaching Faculty Application Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of teaching philosophy A list of three professional references with contact information Graduate and undergraduate transcripts (official transcripts) and background check will be required prior to hire. E-Verify Statement of Participation Goshen College participates in E-Verify. If you are hired, we will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the U.S. Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Statement Goshen College is an equal opportunity employer, committed to enhancing diversity across the institution. Goshen College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity or any legally protected status. As a religious institution, Goshen College expressly reserves its rights, its understandings of, and its commitments to the historic Anabaptist identity and the teachings of Mennonite Church USA, and reserves the legal right to hire and employ individuals who support the values of the college. To protect the welfare and provide for the safety of the students, employees, visitors, and resources of Goshen College, background checks are conducted by the Office of Human Resources on all new and re-hired employees. About Goshen College Goshen College is a nationally-ranked college and Hispanic-Serving Institution in Indiana renowned for its distinctive hands-on, real-world educational opportunities, and its commitment to creating positive change in the community and the world. The college offers over 65 undergraduate areas of study; as well as best-in-class graduate programs in nursing, business administration, social work and environmental education. This caring, safe and diverse campus prides itself on providing excellent academic programs that connect arts with sciences, and theory with practice — exposing students to multiple perspectives and encouraging them to think deeply, live creatively and lead purposefully. The college is located in the City of Goshen in the heart of Elkhart County, within several hours of Chicago, Indianapolis and Detroit. Residents of Goshen enjoy a culturally diverse small-town atmosphere with an active arts community, a vibrant and entrepreneurial downtown, the Maple City Greenway network of bicycle paths and affordable housing prices. Learn more at goodofgoshen.com. Contact HR Human Resources Goshen College 1700 S. Main Street Goshen, IN 46526-4795 E-mail: [email protected] Telephone: (574) 535-7111 Apply Now Academics Menu Toggle Undergraduate Programs Graduate and Licensure Programs Honors Program Global Engagement Academic Dean’s Office Registrar’s Office Admissions and Aid Menu Toggle Undergraduate Admissions Graduate & Licensure Admissions Financial Aid Scholarships Net Price Calculator Visit Athletics Menu Toggle Recruiting Maple Leaf Athletic Club Watch Live Give to MLAC Student Life Menu Toggle Campus Housing Dining Clubs and Extracurriculars Campus Ministries Campus Safety Center for Health & Wellness About Menu Toggle Who We Are News and Events Facilities and Centers Employment Give to Goshen College Contact Us and Campus 