    "https://www.goshen.edu/employment/part-time-campus-safety-officer/": {
      "title": "Part-Time Campus Safety Officer",
      "description": "Part-Time Campus Safety Officer - Goshen College Skip to Main Content Language Toggle Select Language English Spanish French Portuguese Chinese (Simplified) Search Toggle Search our site Search Menu Menu Toggle Apply Get Info Visit Give New Students Parents & Families Alumni Community Academics Menu Toggle Undergraduate Programs Graduate and Licensure Programs Honors Program Global Engagement Academic Dean’s Office Registrar’s Office Admissions and Aid Menu Toggle Undergraduate Admissions Graduate & Licensure Admissions Financial Aid Scholarships Net Price Calculator Visit Athletics Menu Toggle Recruiting Maple Leaf Athletic Club Watch Live Give to MLAC Student Life Menu Toggle Campus Housing Dining Clubs and Extracurriculars Campus Ministries Campus Safety Center for Health & Wellness About Menu Toggle Who We Are News and Events Facilities and Centers Employment Give to Goshen College Contact Us and Campus Directory Employment Open Position Part-Time Campus Safety Officer Apply Here Goshen College is a Christian liberal arts institution that prepares students to thrive in life, leadership and service. We strive to model an inclusive community committed to transformative justice, peace, and sustainability. A respect and appreciation of the Anabaptist- Mennonite faith perspective and practices, and a commitment to the mission, vision, core values and community standards of Goshen College, are important for teaching and administrative faculty members. Position Summary: Goshen College is hiring part-time Campus Safety Officers to provide patrol coverage and fill open shifts across campus. Officers are to be a visible presence on campus, and the role is built around service and “Community Care-taking.” Some of the duties performed are assisting students, staff, faculty, and visitors, securing buildings, responding to incidents, and documenting what happens. Shifts may be variable lengths up to 12 hours and include evenings, overnights, weekends, and holidays. Pay is $15.25/hr. Key Responsibilities: Conduct foot and vehicle patrols of campus buildings, grounds, and parking areas Lock, unlock, and secure buildings on schedule; verify doors and access points Respond to calls for service, alarms, medical incidents, and emergencies, and request police, fire, or EMS support as needed Write clear, accurate, and timely incident reports and shift activity logs Assist community members with escorts, lockouts, and general questions Enforce parking and campus policies Monitor camera, alarm, and access control systems and report equipment problems Provide coverage, access control, and traffic support for campus events as assigned Maintain communication with on-duty staff and follow department protocols Required Qualifications: High school diploma or GED Valid driver’s license and an insurable driving record Basic computer skills, including email and web-based reporting Ability to write clear, factual reports Ability to work independently, take initiative, and use sound judgment with limited supervision Ability to interact effectively with a diverse college community Successful completion of a background check Preferred Qualifications: Experience in security, law enforcement, military, corrections, EMS, healthcare, education, or customer-facing service work Current First Aid/CPR/AED certification, or willingness to obtain one Experience with conflict resolution Familiarity with higher education or residential communities Conversational Spanish Physical Requirements: Officers must be able to walk and stand for extended periods, patrol outdoors in all weather, climb stairs, lift and carry up to 40 pounds, and move quickly to respond to campus emergencies. How to Apply Application materials may be attached to the Professional Staff & Staff Application or sent electronically to hr@goshen.edu . Required: Complete the online Professional Staff & Staff Application Cover letter Resume A list of 3 professional references with contact information E-Verify Statement of Participation Goshen College participates in E-Verify. If you are hired, we will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the U.S. Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Statement Goshen College is an equal opportunity employer, committed to enhancing diversity across the institution. Goshen College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity or any legally protected status. As a religious institution, Goshen College expressly reserves its rights, its understandings of, and its commitments to the historic Anabaptist identity and the teachings of Mennonite Church USA, and reserves the legal right to hire and employ individuals who support the values of the college. To protect the welfare and provide for the safety of the students, employees, visitors, and resources of Goshen College, background checks are conducted by the Office of Human Resources on all new and re-hired employees. About Goshen College Goshen College is a nationally-ranked college and Hispanic-Serving Institution in Indiana renowned for its distinctive hands-on, real-world educational opportunities, and its commitment to creating positive change in the community and the world. The college offers over 65 undergraduate areas of study; as well as best-in-class graduate programs in nursing, business administration, social work and environmental education. This caring, safe and diverse campus prides itself on providing excellent academic programs that connect arts with sciences, and theory with practice — exposing students to multiple perspectives and encouraging them to think deeply, live creatively and lead purposefully. The college is located in the City of Goshen in the heart of Elkhart County, within several hours of Chicago, Indianapolis and Detroit. Residents of Goshen enjoy a culturally diverse small-town atmosphere with an active arts community, a vibrant and entrepreneurial downtown, the Maple City Greenway network of bicycle paths and affordable housing prices. Learn more at goodofgoshen.com. Contact HR Human Resources Goshen College 1700 S. Main Street Goshen, IN 46526-4795 E-mail: hr@goshen.edu Telephone: (574) 535-7111 Apply Now Academics Menu Toggle Undergraduate Programs Graduate and Licensure Programs Honors Program Global Engagement Academic Dean’s Office Registrar’s Office Admissions and Aid Menu Toggle Undergraduate Admissions Graduate & Licensure Admissions Financial Aid Scholarships Net Price Calculator Visit Athletics Menu Toggle Recruiting Maple Leaf Athletic Club Watch Live Give to MLAC Student Life Menu Toggle Campus Housing Dining Clubs and Extracurriculars Campus Ministries Campus Safety Center for Health & Wellness About Menu Toggle Who We Are News and Events Facilities and Centers Employment Give to Goshen College Contact Us and Campus Directory Address 1700 South Main Street Goshen, IN 46526 Get directions Phone Directory News & Events Employment Give Athletics New Students MyGC Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Title IX Website Feedback Form © 2026\t\tGoshen College Alert JavaScript is disabled This site requires JavaScript to function properly. We use cookies Our site uses cookies to enhance your site experience in accordance with our privacy policy . By continuing to use our site, you agree to our use of cookies. OK We use cookies Our site uses cookies to enhance your site experience in accordance with our privacy policy . By continuing to use our site, you agree to our use of cookies. Google reCAPTCHA response"
